---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const body = "<section class=\"hero wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">// Services</span><span class=\"folio\">01</span></div> </div> <h1 class=\"h1 reveal d1\" style=\"max-width:22ch;margin-top:18px;font-size:clamp(32px,4.4vw,60px)\">WordPress Development from Indonesia — Built to Hand Over, Not to Hold Hostage</h1> <p class=\"lead reveal d2\" style=\"margin-top:22px\">Clean WordPress builds for international clients, from someone who has spent six years working across time zones and knows what actually goes wrong.</p> <div class=\"reveal d3\" style=\"margin-top:32px;display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap\"> <a href=\"https://wa.me/6285927277560?text=Hi!%20I'd%20like%20to%20talk%20about%20a%20WordPress%20project...\" class=\"btn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-wa=\"hero\" data-page=\"/en/services/wordpress-development.html\"> Free Consultation<span class=\"arr\">↗</span> </a> <a href=\"/en/contact\" class=\"btn ghost\">Contact me <span class=\"arr\">↗</span></a> </div> </section> <hr class=\"hair\" style=\"margin:0 var(--gut)\"> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">// 02 — The problem</span><span class=\"folio\">02</span></div> </div> <div class=\"persp\"> <div class=\"reveal\"><p class=\"big\">The real risk in hiring offshore isn&#39;t the rate.</p></div> <div class=\"reveal d1\"> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-bottom:20px\">Most people considering a developer in Southeast Asia are quietly weighing one thing: what happens if this goes wrong. Not the price — the recovery cost. The rate looks attractive until you imagine explaining to your board why the site is half-finished and the developer has stopped replying.</p><p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-bottom:20px\">That fear is usually well-founded, but it is aimed at the wrong target. The projects I have been called in to rescue did not fail because the developer was offshore. They failed because nobody wrote down what was being built, nobody owned the licences, and nobody could read the code afterwards.</p><p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-bottom:20px\">So I build with the assumption that you will eventually want to leave. Licences in your name. Hosting in your account. As few plugins as possible. A structure the next developer can read without calling me. If that makes me easier to replace, good — that is the point.</p> </div> </div> </section> <hr class=\"hair\" style=\"margin:0 var(--gut)\"> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div><span class=\"eyebrow\">// 03 — What's included</span><h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px;max-width:20ch\">What you actually get.</h2></div> <span class=\"folio\">03</span> </div> </div> <div class=\"deflist reveal\"> <div><b>Clean setup</b><p>No multipurpose theme, no overlapping plugins. Only what the project actually uses.</p></div><div><b>Content modelling</b><p>Custom post types and fields shaped around your content, so adding to it feels obvious rather than improvised.</p></div><div><b>Performance</b><p>Images, caching, and asset loading handled during the build — not patched with a plugin at the end.</p></div><div><b>Technical SEO</b><p>Heading structure, schema, sitemap, and URLs correct from day one.</p></div><div><b>Full ownership</b><p>Domain, hosting, and licences in your name. I help set them up; the accounts are yours.</p></div><div><b>Documentation &amp; handover</b><p>A recorded walkthrough and written notes, so whoever inherits this has something to work from.</p></div><div><b>Overlap hours</b><p>I work GMT+7 and keep deliberate overlap with European mornings. Async by default, with written updates you can read on your schedule.</p></div> </div> </section> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div> <span class=\"eyebrow\">// 04 — Fit</span> <h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px;max-width:22ch\">Who this is for — and who it isn't.</h2> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-top:16px;max-width:62ch\">The right column matters as much as the left. I would rather lose the project here than have us both discover it in week five.</p> </div> <span class=\"folio\">04</span> </div> </div> <div class=\"fit-grid reveal\"> <div class=\"fit yes\"><b>A good fit if</b><ul><li>Organisations that want to own their digital assets outright.</li><li>Sites whose content will keep growing — articles, programmes, publications.</li><li>Teams that want to manage their own content without a developer.</li><li>Existing WordPress sites that have become slow and frightening to touch.</li></ul></div> <div class=\"fit no\"><b>Not a fit if</b><ul><li>You need someone online in your working hours all day. I keep overlap, not full coverage, and pretending otherwise would only fail you later.</li><li>You want to keep the multipurpose theme you already have. If that is a condition, I am the wrong person.</li><li>You are hiring purely on rate. There is always someone cheaper, and you would be buying the exact risk you are trying to avoid.</li><li>Nobody will maintain anything after launch. WordPress needs light but regular care.</li></ul></div> </div> </section> <hr class=\"hair\" style=\"margin:0 var(--gut)\"> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div> <span class=\"eyebrow\">// 05 — Process</span> <h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px\">How this runs.</h2> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-top:16px;max-width:62ch\">3–6 weeks for a new site. Redesigns with content migration usually take longer, depending on how much legacy content exists.</p> </div> <span class=\"folio\">05</span> </div> </div> <div class=\"proc\"> <div class=\"proc-step reveal\"><div class=\"pn\">1.</div><h3>Audit or discovery</h3><p>If a site exists: what can be salvaged, what has to go. If not: content structure first.</p></div><div class=\"proc-step reveal\"><div class=\"pn\">2.</div><h3>Structure &amp; design</h3><p>Content model and page hierarchy agreed before any visual work begins.</p></div><div class=\"proc-step reveal\"><div class=\"pn\">3.</div><h3>Build &amp; migrate</h3><p>Theme development, content migration, and redirect mapping if URLs change — so existing rankings survive.</p></div><div class=\"proc-step reveal\"><div class=\"pn\">4.</div><h3>Launch &amp; hand over</h3><p>Access, licences, and documentation transferred fully to you.</p></div> </div> </section> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div> <span class=\"eyebrow\">// 06 — Pricing</span> <h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px\">From IDR 5,000,000 (approx. USD 320)</h2> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-top:16px;max-width:62ch\">Indicative conversion only; quoted and invoiced in IDR. Depends on page count, content structure, and whether there is a migration.</p> <div style=\"margin-top:26px\"><a href=\"/en/contact\" class=\"btn ghost\">Contact me <span class=\"arr\">↗</span></a></div> </div> <span class=\"folio\">06</span> </div> </div> </section> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div><span class=\"eyebrow\">// 07 — Examples</span><h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px\">Comparable work.</h2></div> <span class=\"folio\">07</span> </div> </div> <div class=\"more-grid reveal\"> <a class=\"more-card\" href=\"https://jakartafeminist.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> <div class=\"mthumb\"><img src=\"/img/work/jakarta-feminist.webp\" alt=\"Screenshot of the Jakarta Feminist project\" width=\"1200\" height=\"579\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div> <div class=\"mt\"><h3 class=\"h3\">Jakarta Feminist</h3><span class=\"mtag\">.Redesign .WordPress</span></div> <p>A feminist organisation strengthening its advocacy. I consolidated editorial content, events, and resources into a single mobilisation hub — migrating from Wix Editor to WordPress, supporting Women&#39;s March Jakarta, FemFest, and more.</p> <span class=\"open\">View site ↗</span> </a><a class=\"more-card\" href=\"https://ipasindonesia.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> <div class=\"mthumb\"><img src=\"/img/work/ipas-indonesia.webp\" alt=\"Screenshot of the Ipas Indonesia project\" width=\"947\" height=\"857\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div> <div class=\"mt\"><h3 class=\"h3\">Ipas Indonesia</h3><span class=\"mtag\">.Redesign .WordPress</span></div> <p>A reproductive health NGO expanding access to safe post-abortion care. Their old site had drifted away from the new international design system. I rebuilt it to align with the global brand without sacrificing what the Indonesian audience responds to.</p> <span class=\"open\">View site ↗</span> </a><a class=\"more-card\" href=\"https://carilayanan.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> <div class=\"mthumb\"><img src=\"/img/work/cari-layanan.webp\" alt=\"Screenshot of the Cari Layanan project\" width=\"861\" height=\"822\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div> <div class=\"mt\"><h3 class=\"h3\">Cari Layanan</h3><span class=\"mtag\">.WordPress</span></div> <p>A crisis directory for survivors of gender-based violence during COVID-19. I built a WordPress directory mapping verified services by location and need — confidential, immediately accessible, and able to scale to thousands of users.</p> <span class=\"open\">View site ↗</span> </a> </div> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-top:24px;font-size:15px\"> <a href=\"/en/work\" style=\"text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px\">See the full portfolio</a> — with the reasoning behind each decision.\n</p> </section> <hr class=\"hair\" style=\"margin:0 var(--gut)\"> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div><span class=\"eyebrow\">// 08 — Questions</span><h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px\">What people usually ask.</h2></div> <span class=\"folio\">08</span> </div> </div> <div class=\"faq reveal\"> <details> <summary><span class=\"fq\">/01</span>How do you handle the time difference?</summary> <p class=\"fa\">I work GMT+7, which overlaps with European mornings and does not overlap much with the Americas. I treat that as a constraint to design around rather than hide: written updates you can read whenever, decisions batched instead of drip-fed, and scheduled calls inside the overlap. In practice most clients find fewer, better-prepared calls preferable to constant availability.</p> </details><details> <summary><span class=\"fq\">/02</span>Can you migrate from Wix, Squarespace, or another platform?</summary> <p class=\"fa\">Yes — Jakarta Feminist was a Wix Editor to WordPress migration. The part that decides whether a migration succeeds is not moving the content, it is mapping old URLs to new ones with correct redirects. Skip that and years of accumulated ranking can disappear overnight.</p> </details><details> <summary><span class=\"fq\">/03</span>What happens if I want to move to another developer?</summary> <p class=\"fa\">You can, without asking me. Domain, hosting, and licences are in your name from the start, and the build is deliberately readable by someone else. A site only its author can touch is not an asset — it is a trap, and I do not build them.</p> </details><details> <summary><span class=\"fq\">/04</span>Is the lower rate reflected in the quality?</summary> <p class=\"fa\">The rate reflects where I live, not how I work. Costs in Indonesia are lower than in London or Sydney, so the same work costs you less without costing me more. What you should actually check is the work itself — the portfolio on this site includes clients in Tanzania, Mumbai, London, and Jakarta, and you can visit every one of them.</p> </details> </div> </section> <section class=\"cta-ink pad\"> <img class=\"bgimg\" src=\"/img/cta-bg.webp\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1024\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> <div class=\"wrap\" style=\"position:relative\"> <span class=\"eyebrow reveal\">// Let's talk</span> <h2 class=\"h2 reveal d1\" style=\"margin:24px 0 36px;max-width:20ch\">Sounds like a fit? Let's test that first.</h2> <div class=\"reveal d2\"> <a href=\"https://wa.me/6285927277560?text=Hi!%20I'd%20like%20to%20talk%20about%20a%20WordPress%20project...\" class=\"btn on-ink\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-wa=\"cta\" data-page=\"/en/services/wordpress-development.html\"> Free Consultation<span class=\"arr\">↗</span> </a> </div> </div> </section>";
const extraSchema = [{"@type":"Service","name":"wordpress developer indonesia","description":"WordPress development from Indonesia for international clients. Full ownership, clean builds, no lock-in. English-speaking, 6+ years across global markets.","url":"https://haloglory.com/en/services/wordpress-development","serviceType":"WordPress Development","provider":{"@id":"https://haloglory.com/#service"},"areaServed":{"@type":"Country","name":"Indonesia"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://haloglory.com/en"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Services","item":"https://haloglory.com/en/services"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"WordPress Development","item":"https://haloglory.com/en/services/wordpress-development"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do you handle the time difference?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I work GMT+7, which overlaps with European mornings and does not overlap much with the Americas. I treat that as a constraint to design around rather than hide: written updates you can read whenever, decisions batched instead of drip-fed, and scheduled calls inside the overlap. In practice most clients find fewer, better-prepared calls preferable to constant availability."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you migrate from Wix, Squarespace, or another platform?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — Jakarta Feminist was a Wix Editor to WordPress migration. The part that decides whether a migration succeeds is not moving the content, it is mapping old URLs to new ones with correct redirects. Skip that and years of accumulated ranking can disappear overnight."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens if I want to move to another developer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can, without asking me. Domain, hosting, and licences are in your name from the start, and the build is deliberately readable by someone else. A site only its author can touch is not an asset — it is a trap, and I do not build them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the lower rate reflected in the quality?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The rate reflects where I live, not how I work. Costs in Indonesia are lower than in London or Sydney, so the same work costs you less without costing me more. What you should actually check is the work itself — the portfolio on this site includes clients in Tanzania, Mumbai, London, and Jakarta, and you can visit every one of them."}}]}];
